  "parentCard": {
    "title": "Five paper kites, and two that fly away",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "cut-draw",
    "steps": [
      "Draw five kites together on one big sheet, big enough for their hands, and let them colour every one of them their own way.",
      "Cut them out, then count them onto the table one at a time, so they hear you land on five at the end.",
      "Tell the story together: five kites were flying, then two flew away. They pick the two themselves and fly them off the table.",
      "Ask how many are left, then ask them to tell you the whole story back in their own words, from the start.",
      "Ask them to be the storyteller: they tell you a kite story of their own, you fly the kites they name, and they check whether you flew the right number."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "Do they count the ones left from one again, or do they already know how many without counting?",
      "When they tell the story back, does the number that flew away survive in their telling, or do they only say how many are left?",
      "When they choose how many fly away, do they ever choose all of them, and what do they call what is left?"
    ]
  }
